{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"snippet-manager","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Snippet Manager","description":"Keep your own snippets in one place with a page to add, edit, search and delete them. Import and export VS Code snippet files.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Productivity"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:snippetManager.open","onCommand:snippetManager.insert","onCommand:snippetManager.saveSelection","onCommand:snippetManager.exportVsCode","onCommand:snippetManager.importVsCode"],"permissions":[],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"snippetManager.open","title":"Manage Snippets","category":"Snippet Manager"},{"command":"snippetManager.insert","title":"Insert Snippet...","category":"Snippet Manager"},{"command":"snippetManager.saveSelection","title":"Save Selection as Snippet...","category":"Snippet Manager"},{"command":"snippetManager.exportVsCode","title":"Export All as VS Code Snippet JSON","category":"Snippet Manager"},{"command":"snippetManager.importVsCode","title":"Import VS Code Snippet JSON from Selection","category":"Snippet Manager"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"snippetManager.insert","key":"Ctrl+Alt+J"}]}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Snippet Manager: keep your own snippets in one place, with a page to add, edit, search and delete them.\n// Insert one from the palette, or export all of them as a VS Code snippet file. No permissions: they live in the extension's own storage.\n\nconst KEY = 'snippets.v2';\nconst MAX = 400;\n\n/** Removes tab stops from a snippet body: ${1:name} becomes name, $1 and $0 disappear, \\$ becomes a dollar sign. */\nfunction plain(body) {\n  return String(body)\n    .replace(/\\\\\\$/g, '\\u0000')\n    .replace(/\\$\\{\\d+:([^}]*)\\}/g, '$1')\n    .replace(/\\$\\{\\d+\\}/g, '')\n    .replace(/\\$\\d+/g, '')\n    .replace(/\\u0000/g, '$');\n}\n\nconst clean = (s) => ({\n  id: String(s.id || Date.now().toString(36) + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 6)).slice(0, 40),\n  name: String(s.name || '').trim().slice(0, 80),\n  prefix: String(s.prefix || '').trim().replace(/\\s+/g, '').slice(0, 40),\n  lang: String(s.lang || '').trim().slice(0, 40),\n  body: String(s.body || '').slice(0, 20000),\n});\n\n/** VS Code snippet file format: { \"Name\": { \"prefix\": \"...\", \"body\": [\"line\", ...], \"scope\": \"javascript\" } }. */\nfunction toVsCode(list) {\n  const out = {};\n  for (const s of list) {\n    let name = s.name || s.prefix;\n    for (let i = 2; name in out; i++) name = (s.name || s.prefix) + ' ' + i;\n    out[name] = { prefix: s.prefix || s.name, body: s.body.split('\\n'), ...(s.lang ? { scope: s.lang } : {}) };\n  }\n  return JSON.stringify(out, null, 2);\n}\n\nfunction fromVsCode(text) {\n  const raw = JSON.parse(text);\n  const out = [];\n  for (const [name, v] of Object.entries(raw)) {\n    if (!v || typeof v !== 'object') continue;\n    const body = Array.isArray(v.body) ? v.body.join('\\n') : String(v.body || '');\n    const prefix = Array.isArray(v.prefix) ? v.prefix[0] : v.prefix;\n    if (!body) continue;\n    out.push(clean({ name, prefix: prefix || name, lang: v.scope || '', body }));\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\nconst esc = (s) => String(s).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/\"/g, '&quot;');\n\nfunction page(list) {\n  return `<style>\n  body { font-family: var(--ui); } h3 { margin: 0 0 10px; }\n  input, textarea, select { width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; background: var(--raised, transparent); color: var(--fg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 7px 9px; font: 13px var(--ui); outline: none; } input:focus, textarea:focus { border-color: var(--accent); }\n  textarea { font: 12px/1.5 var(--mono, monospace); min-height: 150px; resize: vertical; }\n  button { background: var(--raised, transparent); color: var(--fg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 5px; padding: 5px 12px; cursor: pointer; } button:hover { border-color: var(--accent); } button.go { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; border-color: var(--accent); }\n  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(180px, 1fr) minmax(280px, 1.4fr); gap: 18px; align-items: start; } @media (max-width: 640px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }\n  .row { padding: 8px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 7px; margin-bottom: 6px; cursor: pointer; } .row:hover, .row.on { border-color: var(--accent); }\n  .row b { display: block; } .row span { color: var(--fg-dim); font-size: 12px; } .dim { color: var(--fg-dim); font-size: 12px; }\n  label { display: block; font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-dim); margin: 10px 0 3px; } .bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-top: 12px; }\n  code { font-family: var(--mono, monospace); background: var(--raised, rgba(128,128,128,.2)); padding: 0 4px; border-radius: 3px; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"grid\">\n  <div><h3>Your snippets <span class=\"dim\" id=\"count\"></span></h3><input id=\"q\" placeholder=\"Search\"><div id=\"list\" style=\"margin-top:10px\"></div><div class=\"bar\"><button id=\"new\">New snippet</button></div></div>\n  <div><h3 id=\"title\">New snippet</h3>\n    <label>Name</label><input id=\"name\" placeholder=\"Fetch with error handling\">\n    <label>Prefix: what you type to find it</label><input id=\"prefix\" placeholder=\"fetchx\">\n    <label>Language (optional, for example JavaScript or Python)</label><input id=\"lang\" placeholder=\"Any language\">\n    <label>Text</label><textarea id=\"body\" spellcheck=\"false\" placeholder=\"Write the snippet text. You can paste code.\"></textarea>\n    <div class=\"dim\" style=\"margin-top:6px\">Tab stops like <code>\\${1:name}</code> are kept when you export to VS Code, and removed when you insert here.</div>\n    <div class=\"bar\"><button class=\"go\" id=\"save\">Save</button><button id=\"del\">Delete</button><button id=\"ins\">Insert into file</button></div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<script>\n  let items = ${JSON.stringify(list).replace(/</g, '\\\\u003c')};\n  let cur = null;\n  const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\n  function render() {\n    const q = $('q').value.toLowerCase();\n    $('count').textContent = '(' + items.length + ')';\n    $('list').innerHTML = '';\n    for (const s of items.filter((s) => !q || (s.name + ' ' + s.prefix + ' ' + s.body).toLowerCase().includes(q))) {\n      const d = document.createElement('div');\n      d.className = 'row' + (cur === s.id ? ' on' : '');\n      const b = document.createElement('b'); b.textContent = s.name || s.prefix;\n      const sp = document.createElement('span'); sp.textContent = s.prefix + (s.lang ? '  ·  ' + s.lang : '');\n      d.append(b, sp);\n      d.onclick = () => { cur = s.id; $('title').textContent = 'Edit snippet'; $('name').value = s.name; $('prefix').value = s.prefix; $('lang').value = s.lang; $('body').value = s.body; render(); };\n      $('list').appendChild(d);\n    }\n    if (!items.length) $('list').innerHTML = '<div class=\"dim\">No snippets yet. Write one on the right, or run \"Save Selection as Snippet\" in the editor.</div>';\n  }\n  function form() { return { id: cur, name: $('name').value, prefix: $('prefix').value, lang: $('lang').value, body: $('body').value }; }\n  function reset() { cur = null; $('title').textContent = 'New snippet'; for (const id of ['name', 'prefix', 'lang', 'body']) $('' + id).value = ''; render(); }\n  $('q').oninput = render;\n  $('new').onclick = reset;\n  $('save').onclick = () => ferrumPanel.postMessage({ type: 'save', snippet: form() });\n  $('del').onclick = () => { if (cur) ferrumPanel.postMessage({ type: 'delete', id: cur }); };\n  $('ins').onclick = () => ferrumPanel.postMessage({ type: 'insert', body: $('body').value });\n  ferrumPanel.onMessage((m) => { if (m.type === 'list') { items = m.items; if (m.select !== undefined) cur = m.select; if (m.reset) reset(); else render(); } });\n  render();\n</script>`;\n}\n\nexports._test = { plain, clean, toVsCode, fromVsCode };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  let panel = null;\n  const reg = (id, fn) => context.subscriptions.push(ferrum.commands.register(id, fn));\n  const load = async () => (await ferrum.storage.get(KEY, [])).filter((s) => s && s.body);\n  const save = (list) => ferrum.storage.set(KEY, list.slice(0, MAX));\n\n  async function upsert(raw) {\n    const s = clean(raw);\n    if (!s.body.trim()) throw new Error('The snippet has no text.');\n    if (!s.prefix) s.prefix = (s.name || 'snippet').toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '').slice(0, 12) || 'snip';\n    if (!s.name) s.name = s.prefix;\n    const list = await load();\n    const i = list.findIndex((x) => x.id === raw.id);\n    if (i >= 0) list[i] = { ...s, id: raw.id };\n    else if (list.length >= MAX) throw new Error('You can keep ' + MAX + ' snippets.');\n    else list.unshift(s);\n    await save(list);\n    return i >= 0 ? raw.id : s.id;\n  }\n\n  async function open() {\n    const html = page(await load());\n    if (panel) return panel.setHtml(html);\n    panel = await ferrum.window.showPanel({ title: 'Snippets', html });\n    panel.onDidClose(() => (panel = null));\n    panel.onMessage(async (m) => {\n      try {\n        if (m.type === 'save') {\n          const id = await upsert(m.snippet || {});\n          panel.postMessage({ type: 'list', items: await load(), select: id });\n        } else if (m.type === 'delete') {\n          await save((await load()).filter((s) => s.id !== m.id));\n          panel.postMessage({ type: 'list', items: await load(), reset: true });\n        } else if (m.type === 'insert') {\n          const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n          if (!doc) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a file to insert into.', 'warn');\n          await ferrum.editor.insert(plain(String(m.body || '')));\n        }\n      } catch (e) {\n        ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'warn');\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  reg('snippetManager.open', open);\n\n  reg('snippetManager.insert', async () => {\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (!doc) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a file first.', 'warn');\n    const list = await load();\n    if (!list.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('You have no snippets yet. Run \"Snippets: Manage\" to add some.');\n    const lang = String(doc.language || '').toLowerCase();\n    const fits = list.filter((s) => !s.lang || s.lang.toLowerCase() === lang);\n    const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick((fits.length ? fits : list).map((s) => ({ label: s.name, detail: s.body.split('\\n')[0].slice(0, 100), description: s.prefix + (s.lang ? ' · ' + s.lang : ''), body: s.body })), { placeholder: 'Insert a snippet' });\n    if (!pick) return;\n    // Keep the indentation of the current line for the lines after the first.\n    const line = await ferrum.editor.getLine(doc.selection.start.line);\n    const indent = /^\\s*/.exec(line)[0];\n    await ferrum.editor.insert(plain(pick.body).split('\\n').map((l, i) => (i ? indent + l : l)).join('\\n'));\n  });\n\n  reg('snippetManager.saveSelection', async () => {\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (!doc || !doc.selectedText) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Select the text to keep as a snippet.', 'warn');\n    const name = ((await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Name of the snippet' })) || '').trim();\n    if (!name) return;\n    const prefix = ((await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Prefix: what you will type to find it', value: name.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '').slice(0, 10) })) || '').trim();\n    if (!prefix) return;\n    // Remove the indentation of the first line from all lines, so the snippet can be put anywhere.\n    const lines = doc.selectedText.split('\\n');\n    const min = Math.min(...lines.filter((l) => l.trim()).map((l) => /^[ \\t]*/.exec(l)[0].length));\n    try {\n      await upsert({ name, prefix, lang: doc.language || '', body: lines.map((l) => l.slice(Math.min(min, /^[ \\t]*/.exec(l)[0].length))).join('\\n') });\n      ferrum.window.showMessage('Saved snippet \"' + name + '\".');\n      if (panel) panel.postMessage({ type: 'list', items: await load() });\n    } catch (e) {\n      ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'warn');\n    }\n  });\n\n  reg('snippetManager.exportVsCode', async () => {\n    const list = await load();\n    if (!list.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('You have no snippets to export.');\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (!doc) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open an empty file, then run this again to put the JSON in it.', 'warn');\n    await ferrum.editor.insert(toVsCode(list));\n  });\n\n  reg('snippetManager.importVsCode', async () => {\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (!doc || !doc.selectedText) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Select the JSON of a VS Code snippet file first.', 'warn');\n    try {\n      const incoming = fromVsCode(doc.selectedText);\n      if (!incoming.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('No snippets found in that JSON.', 'warn');\n      const list = await load();\n      await save([...incoming, ...list]);\n      ferrum.window.showMessage('Imported ' + incoming.length + ' snippet' + (incoming.length === 1 ? '' : 's') + '.');\n      if (panel) panel.postMessage({ type: 'list', items: await load() });\n    } catch (e) {\n      ferrum.window.showMessage('That is not a snippet file: ' + e.message, 'warn');\n    }\n  });\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Snippet Manager\n\nYour own library of snippets, with a real page to manage it.\n\n- **Manage Snippets** opens a page: a searchable list on the left, an editor on the right (name, prefix, language, text). Save, delete, or insert into your file.\n- **Save Selection as Snippet...** turns the selected code into a snippet in two prompts, removing the shared indentation.\n- **Insert Snippet...** shows your snippets (the ones for the current language first) in a list; the lines after the first keep the indentation of the line you are on.\n- **Export All as VS Code Snippet JSON** puts them in a file in the standard format, and **Import VS Code Snippet JSON from Selection** reads such a file (select its text first).\n\n## Good to know\n\nThe snippets are kept in this extension's own storage (up to 400, about 1 MB). They are inserted as plain text: tab stops like `${1:name}` are kept when you export but removed when you insert here. For snippets you type a prefix and press Tab for, use a snippet pack extension or `.ferrum/snippets.json`.\n\nNo permissions needed.\n"}}}